  "$comment": "Game definitions (PLAN.md §5). File names are matched case-insensitively; `requiredFiles` entries may list alternatives as `A|B`; `?` and `*` are wildcards in saves/stateFiles. A version is recognised by the SHA-256 of its `files` (at least one executable; the first version whose files all match wins, so a version that needs more files comes before one that needs fewer). `patchVersion`: what patch files call this release in `%version`, only set on releases patches are made for. `kind`: `beta` or `demo` for releases that aren't the full game. `original`: for third-party builds (e.g. copy protection removed), the release they were made from; mods for it are offered, but patches may not fit, unless `repackaged` says the game files are identical. `start` replaces the episode executable at launch (Keen Dreams 1.01/1.13 refuse to run without their START shell). Hashes checked 2026-10-20 against the owner's copies in .local/games/versions.",
